{"kind":"request","text":"Two UI defects reported by hugh against main at 2757411d.\n\nFirst, the header presence strip renders one avatar per session, so a single actor with several live MCP sessions appears many times over: five claude and five codex avatars for two people. Presence answers who is here; it should count people, not processes.\n\nSecond, the UI never says which repository it is showing. A workroom served from one checkout is indistinguishable from one served from another.\n\nConditions of satisfaction: (a) the header shows one avatar per distinct present actor, with the number of that actor's live sessions available on the avatar; (b) the repository path the service is serving is visible in the UI; (c) the widened disclosure is justified in the code by the enforced loopback-only listen, and the existing comment claiming paths are withheld from browser clients is corrected rather than left to lie; (d) UI unit tests cover the presence grouping; (e) make test, make vet and npm run build pass, and the embedded uidist is rebuilt from the changed sources.","body":{"conditions":"One header avatar per distinct present actor with that actor's live session count on it; the served repository path visible in the UI; the loopback-only listen cited in code as the justification and the stale no-paths comment corrected; UI unit tests covering presence grouping; make test, make vet and npm run build passing with uidist rebuilt.","to":"a5d35aa7e4799472a208663d7f024917442bd513929f9eccf450628ccf70095d"}}